; Ellerman's vector journal (Accounting Education 23:5 (2014),
; pp. 496-498) with transaction 2b written in Ledger's cost syntax.  The
; journal is a kernel-checked golden in the ledger-semantics oracle
; (namespace Ledger.Ellerman).  The cost balances the sale at $2000, and
; Ledger leaves the exchange leg that Ellerman books to Equity implicit,
; so the per-commodity totals are $2000 and -20 WIDGET rather than zero.
; This illustrates the @ convention (see opt-equity and regress 1125,
; 1794); it is not a witness for a new balancing rule.

2014/01/01 Beginning vector balance sheet
    Assets          $9000
    Assets          40 WIDGET
    Assets          50 HALF
    Liabilities     $-10000
    Equity          $1000
    Equity          -40 WIDGET
    Equity          -50 HALF

2014/01/02 1. inputs used
    Assets          -30 HALF
    Equity          30 HALF

2014/01/03 2a. widgets produced
    Assets          15 WIDGET
    Equity          -15 WIDGET

2014/01/04 2b. widgets sold, Ledger cost syntax
    Assets          $2000
    Assets          -20 WIDGET @ $100

2014/01/05 3. loan principal
    Assets          $-800
    Liabilities     $800

test bal --flat
              $10200
             20 HALF
           35 WIDGET  Assets
               $1000
            -20 HALF
          -55 WIDGET  Equity
              $-9200  Liabilities
--------------------
               $2000
          -20 WIDGET
end test
